<!-- vaml_viewer — Sprint 11ab VIEWER-GROWTH sample (dep:S824, Sprint 11ab): the
     CLOSED SURFACES RENDERED LIVE. The four S821/S822/S823/S824 closures all
     resolve + render through the generic renderer (the S222_1/11k-6 RELOAD
     re-demonstrated — proving NO regression from the S824 re-base).

     The sample AUTHORS all four closures in one corpus-shaped doc:

       1. Visibility="Collapsed" (S821 — the WPF ComputeValidateVisibility
          boundary gate). A Rectangle authored Collapsed must NOT render (the
          S207 encoder's SkipCollapsed rule), while its visible sibling does —
          the "closed" closure proves the Collapsed gate lands in the LIVE
          renderer.

       2. a panel Opacity="0.75" with a child (S822 — the compositor subtree
          model). The S208 encoder's effective_opacity is the visual-ancestor
          chain PRODUCT, so the child under the 0.75 panel renders at 0.75 × its
          own (compositor subtree alpha), and the panel itself renders at 0.75.

       3. RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5" + an authored RotateTransform
          Angle="45" (S823 — the WPF-faithful Transform-object DP). The S208
          encoder resolves the authored Transform's matrix() and folds the
          RenderTransformOrigin about the fraction center (WPF ArrangeCore);
          the rotated rectangle's emitted item carries a NON-identity Model +
          a dynamic clip to its render slot.

       4. FE-branch alignment/Width/Height authors on a FrameworkElement-branch
          control (S824 — the layout-slot re-key). A Rectangle (FrameworkElement-
          derived) authors Width/Height + Horizontal/VerticalAlignment; these
          resolve under owner "FrameworkElement" (their WPF home) and constrain
          its final_rect.

     The LIVE window display is the [both-apps, not CI] on-machine gate; the
     SEAM (vaml_viewer/viewer_growth_11ab.h + its headless test) is the CI-
     checkable half of the exact code path. ADR-021 consumer path. NO MINIMAL
     REAL. ADR-018 ZERO new locks. -->

<StackPanel xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
            x:Name="Root" Width="640" Height="520" Margin="6"
            Background="#F0F0F0">
  <TextBlock Text="11ab — the closed surfaces render live"
             FontSize="16" Margin="4"/>

  <!-- Closure 1 (S821): Visibility=Collapsed — ColRect must NOT render, while
       its visible sibling VisRect does (the generic-renderer Collapsed gate). -->
  <StackPanel Orientation="0" Margin="4">
    <Rectangle x:Name="ColRect" Width="180" Height="40" Margin="2"
               Visibility="Collapsed" Fill="#FF0000"/>
    <Rectangle x:Name="VisRect" Width="180" Height="40" Margin="2"
               Visibility="Visible" Fill="#00FF00"/>
  </StackPanel>

  <!-- Closure 2 (S822): a panel Opacity=0.75 with a child Opacity=0.8 — the
       compositor subtree model. OpPanel renders at 0.75 (its own); OpChild
       renders at 0.75 × its own 0.8 = 0.6 — effective_opacity is the visual-
       ancestor chain PRODUCT (the WPF base.VisualOpacity composition). -->
  <StackPanel x:Name="OpPanel" Opacity="0.75" Orientation="0" Margin="4"
              Width="320" Height="72" Background="#808080">
    <Rectangle x:Name="OpChild" Width="200" Height="44" Margin="2"
               Opacity="0.8" Fill="#0000FF"/>
  </StackPanel>

  <!-- Closure 3 (S823): RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5" + an authored
       RotateTransform Angle="45" — the Transform-object DP. RotRect's emitted
       item carries the folded rotation about its fraction center. -->
  <Rectangle x:Name="RotRect" Width="120" Height="120" Margin="4"
             Fill="#FFAA00" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
    <Rectangle.RenderTransform>
      <RotateTransform Angle="45"/>
    </Rectangle.RenderTransform>
  </Rectangle>

  <!-- Closure 4 (S824): FE-branch alignment/Width/Height on a FrameworkElement-
       branch control (Rectangle : FrameworkElement). FeRect resolves Width/
       Height/HAlignment/VAlignment under owner "FrameworkElement" and the
       authored Width constrains its final_rect. -->
  <Rectangle x:Name="FeRect" Width="200" Height="50" Margin="4"
             HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top"
             Fill="#FF00FF"/>
</StackPanel>
